        { "type": "text", "text": "Traffic data:", "styles": { "bold": true } },
        { "type": "text", "text": " visitors per variant, traffic source breakdown, conversion rates for each variant", "styles": {} }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "id": "turnin-b4",
      "type": "numberedListItem",
      "props": { "textColor": "default", "backgroundColor": "default", "textAlignment": "left" },
      "content": [
        { "type": "text", "text": "Heatmap or scroll data", "styles": { "bold": true } },
        { "type": "text", "text": " if available (Microsoft Clarity is free and takes 5 minutes to set up)", "styles": {} }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "id": "turnin-b5",
      "type": "numberedListItem",
      "props": { "textColor": "default", "backgroundColor": "default", "textAlignment": "left" },
      "content": [
        { "type": "text", "text": "Winner analysis:", "styles": { "bold": true } },
        { "type": "text", "text": " which framing won? Why do you think so? What does this tell you about how users think about their problem?", "styles": {} }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "id": "turnin-evidence",
      "type": "callout",
      "props": { "emoji": "\u26a0\ufe0f", "textColor": "default", "backgroundColor": "default", "textAlignment": "left" },
      "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "\"We got more clicks on Variant A\" is not an insight. An insight is: \"Users responded to the time-saving framing 3x more than the social framing \u2014 which means they see this as a productivity problem, not a social one. That changes how we should position the product.\"", "styles": {} }],
